  "title": "Gaussian Elimination of Side-Channels: Linear Algebra for Memory Coloring",
  "abstract": "Memory coloring is a software-based technique to ensure microarchitectural isolation between trust domains sharing a CPU. Prior coloring schemes target individual microarchitectural components and thus provide only partial solutions. In this paper, we provide theoretical foundations and practical algorithms to infer comprehensive coloring schemes for modern cloud CPUs.",
